------------------------------------------------------------
VHDL was derived from Ada

Developed for the U.S. Department of Defense, 
both languages aim for reliability, strong typing, 
and hardware/software correctness.

------------------------------------------------------------
Common Keywords between Ada and VHDL
Here’s a table of keywords used in both languages, 
with notes:

Keyword			Purpose

1.) architecture	VHDL: define structure/behavior
					Ada: not used

2.) begin			Start of executable part

3.) end				Close block/entity/process

4.) if, elsif, else	Conditional execution

5.) loop			Repeating block

6.) for				Iteration control

7.) while			Loop condition

8.) exit			Early exit from loop

9.) case, when		Switch/select block

10.) is				Used in declarations/definitions

11.) not, and, or, xor	Boolean logic

12.) then			Used after if condition

13.) procedure		Subprograms

14.) function		Returns a value

15.) return			Return value from function

16.) signal			VHDL: hardware signal
					Ada: used in concurrency

17.) constant		Declare constant

18.) type			Define a new type

19.) subtype		Define constrained subtype

20.) range			Specify range of values

21.) in, out, in out	Parameter modes

22.) use			Visibility of packages/modules

23.) package		Module/namespace

24.) body			Implementation of package or subprogram

25.) null			Empty statement/block

26.) others			Used in case or array assignments


